# Build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OUTPUTS GO TO DRIVE, NOT HERE. Lee's rule, 28 Aug 2026.
# Finished feasibility reports, binders, decks and maps belong in the job's
# folder under G:\My Drive\_Zones\Projects\<year>\<job>\. Before this rule,
# 24MB of Balmain and Karekare artefacts were sitting in this directory,
# which was two thirds of the repository.
#
# Anchored to the root with a leading slash on purpose: templates/ holds
# real assets (stage PNGs, the Zones logo, the A4 deck template) that MUST
# stay tracked. Do not turn these into bare *.png patterns.
/*.pdf
/*.docx
/*.pptx
/*.png
/*.jpg

# CLIENT DATA, READ BEFORE ADDING A REMOTE
# This repository holds the engine only. Real addresses, client names and
# generated reports must never be committed. Adding a remote publishes
# whatever is in here, so check what is staged before you do.

# NO SECOND COPY OF THE CODE, ever. 2 September 2026.
# The installed skill used to hold one and the skill ran THAT, not this tree,
# which is how a fortnight of client S&F decks came out of a stale sf_report.py.
# A third copy was then found here: templates/backup/skill-before-sync-*/ held
# the pre-sync snapshot, i.e. precisely the stale code that caused it, tracked
# and heading for GitHub. Removed; recoverable from commit 342b6b3 if ever
# needed, which it will not be, because git history is the backup now.
templates/backup/skill-before-sync-*/
templates/backup/*/scripts/
